- op: discuss  # 6d79
  at: '2026-09-03T03:07:11Z'  # 6d79
  by: agent  # 6d79
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6d79
  clock: 5  # 6d79
  nonce: 6d79  # 6d79
  message: "SHAPE B SHIPPED (structure closed; measured corpus delta ZERO, reported as a\nceiling like shape A).\n\nWHAT LANDED. resolve_var_field_chain added to the shared TreeSitterAnalyzer --\nthe var-rooted sibling of resolve_receiver_type, which is self-rooted only by\ncontract. Root h -> Holder via _var_types, field f -> File via the struct\nfield-type registry, the exact walk Go's _resolve_field_chain does. Wired into\nrust.py's shape-B block: when Strategy 1.5 left field_receiver_type None (non-\nself root) and the receiver is a field_expression, the var-rooted walk sets it,\nfeeding the existing #595-style module-slot recovery unchanged. Additive\n(nothing else calls it), SLOT-only (has_explicit_binding untouched), so emission\nis byte-identical and no first-party calls edge is minted.\n\nMEASUREMENT, and it is honest zero. The item predicted \"the measured delta is\nsmall BY DESIGN\" because only the field-type-IS-catalogued subset is\nrecoverable. On this corpus that subset is EMPTY:\n  - Edge-level A/B on spacedrive, patch confirmed engaging by a 2,461x call\n    trace (the io-boundaries CLI does NOT re-run the analyzer in-process, so my\n    first A/B measured nothing -- a class-method patch is invisible there;\n    analyze_rust engages it, which is the correct instrument).\n  - resolve_var_field_chain resolves 811 field chains on spacedrive; 0\n    io-boundary classifications change.\n  - Resolved types: Option 208, Vec 145, String 87, HashMap 62, PathBuf 53,\n    AtomicU64 27, serde_json::Value 23, + in-repo structs. The ONLY catalogued\n    hit is Instant x2 -- host_info_read, not a sink.\n  - The write/lock/write_all field-receiver sites here are RwLock/Mutex/watcher\n    fields, NOT std::fs::File. Classifying them would be the false positives the\n    item's own census warned of (spacedrive's 74 lock are Mutex::lock). No\n    genuine File write is dropped -- verified.\n\nSo shape B is correct-by-construction (fixture + 9 branch unit tests) and moves\nzero findings on the sampled corpus. It closes the STRUCTURE of INV-linub's L3\nvar-rooted residual; it pays off the day a repo has a struct field typed\nstd::fs::File that is written. Instrument in-repo:\nscripts/measure-module-matches-arm2-ab.py's sibling, the dizag edge A/B, is a\nsession artifact -- NOT committed (noted as a gap; the analyze_rust edge-diff\nshape is simple enough to rebuild, but a future sizer should commit it).\n\nSTILL OPEN, NOT THIS ITEM: shape C (receiver typed from an external fn's return\nvalue, let c = File::create(..).unwrap()) is WI-lalot -- the type is never\nwritten down, so no field/var walk recovers it."  # 6d79
