  message: "DONE. Both shapes of the struct-field receiver type-drop are closed: shape A (self.field, resolve_receiver_type, shipped 0a35d4bc73) and shape B (var-rooted field chain, resolve_var_field_chain, shipped 59a396395a). The item's diagnosis -- 'a struct-field receiver drops its external type before the module slot is built' -- no longer holds for either self- or var-rooted chains. Shape C (receiver typed from an external fn's return value) was always explicitly out of scope = WI-lalot. Shape B's corpus finding-delta is measured ZERO (spacedrive: 811 field chains resolved, 0 io-boundary changes; the field-receiver sink sites are RwLock/Mutex/watcher fields, not std::fs::File), reported as a ceiling exactly as shape A was -- structure closed, correct-by-construction, pays off when a repo has a File-typed struct field that is written."  # 815c
